{
 "modules": [
  {
   "id": 1,
   "plugin": "Core",
   "model": "Notes",
   "data": {
    "text": "CAMERA MOTION\nPatch any CV (0 to 10 V) into a jack. 0 V is the item's From setting, 10 V its To.\n\nCV-CC 1: MIDI channel 1, CC 81 to 96\n   1 How often the shot changes\n   2 How long each shot lasts\n   3 How the camera is held\n   4 Camera move\n   5 Move speed\n   6 Move follows\n   7 Camera move starts on\n   8 Camera owner\n   9 Move against loudness\n  10 Camera shake while filming\n  11 Speed ramp (speed changing in the shot)\n  12 Slow push in on a face\n  13 The camera circles them\n  14 Turning to reveal\n  15 The camera wanders off\n  16 The stretching background shot\nCV-CC 2: MIDI channel 1, CC 97 to 112\n   1 suite: Handheld hunt\n   2 suite: Smooth push\n   3 suite: Object insert\n   4 suite: Loving camera\n   5 suite: Aggressive camera\n   6 suite: Follows the voice\n   7 suite: Video game camera\n   8 suite: The floor drops\n   9 suite: Something in the room\n  10 suite: Handheld realism\n  11 pair: When the camera goes handheld, gesture grows\n  12 pair: When the player takes the camera, the view becomes theirs\n  13 pair: When a character crosses the room, the camera move starts with them\n  14 pair: When the camera follows a character, it tracks alongside them\n  15 pair: When the camera moves on a breath, a small pause opens up\n  16 pair: When the camera jumps on loud moments, the shot gets shakier\nCV-CC 3: MIDI channel 2, CC 1 to 16\n   1 pair: When the camera turns to reveal a person, it becomes an entrance\n   2 pair: When the camera pushes in on a face, we feel with them\n   3 pair: When the camera pushes in as they realise, the realisation lands\n   4 pair: When the background stretches, we feel it in the body\n   5 pair: When the sound drops out under the stretch, we hear through their ears\n   6 pair: When the camera circles a kiss, tenderness grows\n   7 pair: When the camera whirls around them, the feeling peaks\n   8 pair: When the turn reveals a threat, dread rises\n   9 pair: When the turn is a whip, the picture blurs\n  10 pair: When the camera wanders off to a clue, the audience holds a question\n  11 pair: When the camera wanders off, it lingers where it lands\n  12 pair: When the camera whips to the side, a new neat picture is waiting\n  13 pair: When the camera follows close behind them, we feel what they feel\n  14 pair: When the person panics, the camera shakes more\n  15 pair: When the number peaks, the camera rises above them\n  16 pairs: The camera answers the body\nCV-CC 4: MIDI channel 2, CC 17 to 20\n   1 pairs: Camera moves with a reason\n   2 pairs: The ground gives way\n   3 pairs: Someone is there\n   4 pairs: Handheld realism: the moves"
   },
